<%# The curl example of a Scriptorium upload form: a multipart request with the file's name and type spelled out. Include it with an upload object from uploadCurl in _shared/lab.ts. Every value goes through the escaped output tag. Never put an EJS tag inside an EJS comment: it breaks parsing. %>
<p class="lab-note">From a terminal: <code>curl -F '<%= upload.field %>=@./local-file;filename=&lt;name&gt;;type=&lt;content type&gt;' -F 'caption=&lt;text&gt;' "<%= upload.url %>" -b "hvwa_sid=&lt;copy from devtools&gt;"</code>. Here <code>filename</code> is the name the server receives and <code>type</code> the content type you claim; curl sends exactly what you write. Your lab belongs to your browser session: open this page in your browser, then copy the (HttpOnly) <code>hvwa_sid</code> cookie from the devtools storage into <code>-b</code>. Without it curl starts a different session, and its state and flags will not match yours. The line is bash syntax (Git Bash, WSL, macOS, Linux); in Windows PowerShell write <code>curl.exe</code>, because plain <code>curl</code> there is <code>Invoke-WebRequest</code>.</p>
